(983129, 115074, 2741, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Imagineer:</b></div><hr/><i> I obviously see the lines, but I wonder how interesting this shot is aside of the challenge. In my view if you can produce an image that is printable or hangable then you have achieved something more than simply meet the voters'' satisfaction. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Funny. I have had a lots of success selling my prints to galleries and local newspapers, and have yet to recieve an overall vote of 6.  Personally, I think this is a very interesting photo. A photo being interesting or not generally does not mean it should be hangable or printable. I have seen many ugly photos hanging on walls.<br/> <br/>What it boils down to in this case, and in most cases on this site is, whatever the ''voters'' taste or mood is when voting, determines the vote.<br/> <br/>This should have been in the 5 to 6 average range.<br/> <br/>Good photo.</td>', 'Originally posted by Imagineer: I obviously see the lines, but I wonder how interesting this shot is aside of the challenge. In my view if you can produce an image that is printable or hangable then you have achieved something more than simply meet the voters'' satisfaction.   Funny. I have had a lots of success selling my prints to galleries and local newspapers, and have yet to recieve an overall vote of 6.  Personally, I think this is a very interesting photo. A photo being interesting or not generally does not mean it should be hangable or printable. I have seen many ugly photos hanging on walls. What it boils down to in this case, and in most cases on this site is, whatever the ''voters'' taste or mood is when voting, determines the vote. This should have been in the 5 to 6 average range. Good photo.', '2004-11-01 11:57:36.000000', NULL, 0),
